-438,debrief,debrief,ui.hint,,later q1,app,Notes: Entry preparations delayed by a repeated call,
-439,debrief,debrief,followon.paragraph,,later,g9-systems-drill-required,The extra orbit left the crew facing entry with critically low RCS propellant. A systems-warning drill is required. Choose the other exercise.,
-440,debrief,debrief,debrief,,later,g8-db-later,You chose another orbit to land closer to the recovery force. The crew completed entry with critically low RCS propellant.,
-441,debrief,debrief,debrief,,not q2,g8-db-rework,Calls that needed clarification or repeating delayed the pickup or squeezed the crew's entry preparations. The crew-condition report records the result.,
-442,debrief,debrief,debrief,,later,g8-db-systems-next,Mara's response is recorded above. The next mission must include a systems-warning rehearsal; you'll choose its companion exercise.,
-443,debrief,debrief,debrief,,later,g8-db-departure-later,"Return timing — You took the later opportunity, as history did: Gemini VIII landed in the western Pacific on its seventh revolution and the crew awaited USS Leonard F. Mason. The propellant warning, the closer pickup, and the crew-condition sequence on this route are dramatized, not a reconstruction of that recovery.",
