+455,debrief,debrief,debrief,,crew-blame,g8-db-crew-blame,"You endorsed the criticism of Armstrong and Scott. Cunningham and Stafford's support grew, both crew members lost trust in you, and the astronaut corps became more divided.",
+456,debrief,debrief,ui.heading,,,app,Departures from the record,
+457,debrief,debrief,debrief,,earlier,g8-db-departure-earlier,"Return timing — Historically, Gemini VIII landed in the western Pacific during its seventh revolution and the crew awaited USS Leonard F. Mason. You chose the game's earlier return. The particular ship delay, darkness, crew exhaustion, and rehearsal-dependent pickup sequence are alternate events, not a reconstruction of that recovery.",
+458,debrief,debrief,debrief,,crew-blame,g8-db-departure-blame,"Accountability — Post-flight analysis cleared Armstrong and Scott, while Cunningham and Stafford criticized their handling of the emergency. Kranz instead faulted the ground's lack of docked-flight contingency procedures. You backed the crew's critics. Glen's statement, the increased division, and the changes in astronaut trust are alternate consequences of your choice.",
